# Code owners (https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositories-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners).
# The last matching pattern wins, so the specific paths come after the general ones.
#
# AGENTS.md requires a `security-reviewer` review for every change under shared/protocol/. That role
# is a Claude Code subagent (.claude/agents/security-reviewer.md), not a GitHub account: there is no
# separate user or team to request. The repository owner is therefore the required code owner for
# the protocol, and records the security-reviewer's review in the pull request before approving.
# Enforced only when branch protection has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled.

# Agent <-> console contract (invariant I6): schemas, fixtures, scripts.
